# COVID-19 Vaccination & Mortality Data Analysis (SQL)

## 📌 Overview
This project focuses on analyzing global COVID-19 vaccination and mortality data using SQL to uncover trends, patterns, and key insights from large datasets.

## 🎯 Objective
- Analyze vaccination progress across countries
- Examine COVID-19 death trends over time
- Identify relationships between total cases, deaths, and vaccinations
- Practice data querying and analytical thinking using SQL

## 🛠 Tools & Technologies
- SQL (SSMS)
- Dataset: COVID-19 dataset (Our World in Data / Kaggle)

## 📊 Key Analysis Performed
- Total cases vs total deaths analysis
- Vaccination progress by country
- Death percentage calculation
- Population vs infection rate comparison
- Country-wise and global trend analysis using GROUP BY and aggregations

## 🔍 Sample SQL Operations
- Joins (combining vaccination and death datasets)
- Aggregate functions (SUM, AVG, COUNT)
- Window functions
- Filtering and sorting for trend analysis

## 📈 Key Insights
- Countries with higher vaccination rates showed improved recovery trends over time
- Significant variation observed in infection and mortality rates across regions
- Data highlights the importance of vaccination rollout in controlling death rates

## 📂 Project Structure
- SQL queries file
- Raw dataset

## 🚀 Learning Outcome
- Strengthened SQL skills for real-world data analysis
- Improved ability to extract insights from large datasets
- Built foundation for transitioning into dashboarding and visualization tools 
